Why Does Reversing Work?

Suppose:

a → b → c → d

Twin pairs are:

a ↔ d
b ↔ c

After reversing the second half:

a → b

d → c

Now both lists move in the same direction:

a → b
↑
head

d → c
↑
prev

Therefore:

head.val + prev.val

automatically gives the twin sum.

Complexity Comparison
Approach	Idea	Time	Extra Space
1. ArrayList	Copy values to array	O(n)	O(n)
2. Stack	Store values in reverse order	O(n)	O(n)
3. Reverse 2nd Half	Find middle + reverse + compare	O(n)	O(1)
Best Approach

Approach 3 — Reverse the second half

Because:

Time  = O(n)
Space = O(1)

This is the expected interview solution.

Important Pattern to Remember

This problem is another classic Linked List Fast & Slow Pointer + Reversal problem.

Whenever you see:

"Compare first half with corresponding elements from the end"

Think:

Find Middle
     ↓
Reverse Second Half
     ↓
Compare

This same pattern is extremely useful for:

